{"parentUuid":"cb6949a2-581a-4330-9ec2-4a6a98ccd12a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01U7FQFB3xVueAunxDsTxnQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've read through the four commits, related code, and tests. Here's my review.\n\n## Overall\n\nSolid PR. The three-layered defense (SessionStart hint → transcript-path override → per-session file lock) is well thought out, and the rationale is documented in the right places. Lint clean. The cross-platform filelock is minimal and self-contained. Test coverage is genuinely good — including a concurrent-goroutine convergence test under `-race`.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Layered design with clear authority**: transcript path > hint > caller. The asymmetry between `resolveSessionAgentType` (uses hint) and `correctSessionAgentType` (ignores hint) is deliberate and well-documented (`session_state.go` comment + `manual_commit_hooks.go:2178-2196`).\n- **Path-prefix collision test** in `registry_test.go:212-217` (`\"…/repository/…\"` not matching agent rooted at `\"…/repo\"`) is exactly the kind of edge case I'd want to see covered.\n- **Lock semantics are conservative and fail-open**: `lockErr != nil` proceeds without serialization (`manual_commit_hooks.go:2219`), restoring pre-PR behavior on lock-system failures rather than blocking hooks.\n- **Lock files in a separate `entire-locks/` dir** keeps the existing session enumeration callers (status/doctor/tests) unmodified — explicit in the comment, and the right call.\n- **Banner dedup also covers the Gemini double-fire** (`startup` then `resume`), not just the cross-agent case. The repurposing of `claimedFirst` for two different problems is clean.\n- **Gemini plain-text rationale** (`geminicli/lifecycle.go:21-29`) explains the upstream double-display bug clearly enough that a future maintainer won't \"fix\" it back to JSON.\n\n## Issues\n\n**1. Empty/Unknown agentType at SessionStart silently suppresses the banner** (`lifecycle.go:84-92`).\n\n`StoreAgentTypeHint` returns `created=false, err=nil` when `agentType == \"\" || agentType == AgentTypeUnknown`. The caller sets `claimedFirst = false` for that case (no error → fallback branch isn't taken), and the banner is suppressed even though no agent has actually claimed the session. Probably not reachable in practice today (every registered agent has a non-empty Type), but the comment \"better to duplicate than to suppress\" only protects the error path, not the empty-hint path. Cheap fix: treat the no-op return as `claimedFirst = true`.\n\n**2. `os.Remove` of a held lock file** (`session_state.go:410`).\n\n`ClearSessionState` removes `entire-locks/<sid>.lock` unconditionally. On Unix, unlinking a locked file leaves the in-kernel lock attached to the (now-orphan) inode; a subsequent `Acquire` opens a *new* inode at the same path and gets a separate lock. Practically harmless because ClearSessionState should only run after the session is done, but if a stray hook fires concurrently with cleanup the lock no longer serializes them. Worth a one-line comment acknowledging the assumption, or just don't bother removing the lock file (the dir is small and ignored by other callers).\n\n**3. Lock granularity is narrower than the comment implies.**\n\nThe lock only protects `InitializeSession` against itself. Other paths (`SaveStep`, `SaveTaskStep`, post-commit handlers) don't take it. That's fine for the bug being fixed — both racers in the field are `InitializeSession` callers — but `AcquireSessionLock`'s docstring says \"serialize concurrent processes that initialize the same session,\" which slightly oversells what it covers. If we ever see analogous races elsewhere, we'll need to extend.\n\n**4. No timeout on lock acquisition.**\n\n`flock(LOCK_EX)` / `LockFileEx` block indefinitely. If process A hangs inside `OpenRepository`, process B's hook is stuck. Hooks are short-lived in practice, so this is unlikely to matter, but a context-aware acquire (or a time-bounded attempt with fallback) would be more defensive. Not a blocker.\n\n## Nits\n\n- `registry.go:32` has a stray empty `//` comment line after `// Get retrieves an agent by name.` — looks like a doc removal artifact.\n- `agent_resolution_test.go:181-217`'s concurrent test uses `_ = s.InitializeSession(...)` with a comment defending it. Fine, but it'd be slightly stronger to assert that *at least one* of the two calls returned `nil` (i.e. neither failed for an unrelated reason, e.g. lock dir creation).\n- `correctSessionAgentType` — if `paths.WorktreeRoot` fails, we silently return `(currentType, false)`. Same in `resolveSessionAgentType`. A debug log on the failure path would help future debugging without polluting the happy path.\n\n## Verdict\n\nShip it. The \"empty/Unknown agentType suppresses banner\" path (#1) is the only thing I'd actually want fixed before merge — one-line change. The rest are nits or acknowledgments-of-assumptions, not blockers."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5843,"cache_read_input_tokens":138216,"output_tokens":2221,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2221,"cache_read_input_tokens":138216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaZyUv4HPNca8SFmynRst","type":"assistant","uuid":"64062875-f785-4eaa-b620-9bf1c95b4c45","timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:43:28.287Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c3eb3dfd-f856-4fb0-901f-7bae4034e1d7","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"ashtom/cursor-fix"}
