{"parentUuid":"89d22df1-eea5-4821-864a-e7168f056e18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Su7WFE25nPiSYJc3umfysq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The first-writer-wins hint logic is doing two distinct jobs, and they bundle into the same code path:\n\n**1. Cross-agent disambiguation (the bug this PR fixes)**\n- Cursor IDE forwards a single user prompt to both `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.claude/settings.json`. Two `entire` processes fire SessionStart for the same session_id ~simultaneously. First-writer-wins claims agent ownership for whichever fires first, and the second's banner is suppressed. Without it: two banners per session start, plus the wrong AgentType in `entire status`.\n- Same shape for any future wrapper-style agent (Factory AI Droid → Claude, etc.).\n\n**2. Same-process repeated SessionStart (the Gemini banner dedup)**\n- Gemini fires SessionStart twice in a single process invocation: once for `source=startup`, once for `source=resume`. Without dedup the user sees the banner twice in a single Gemini start. The `Dedupe SessionStart banner per session` commit is specifically about this.\n\n**Unintentionally caught — what we just identified:**\n\n3. **Cross-process resume** — `claude -c`, `cursor-agent --resume <id>`, anything that re-enters an existing `session_id` from a fresh process. The hint persists on disk, so the resumed run never claims, and the banner doesn't appear. Functionally fine, just a UX regression.\n\nSo the dedup logic genuinely serves (1) and (2). Case (3) is collateral. The fix, if you want it, is to gate `claimedFirst` on the SessionStart `source`/`reason` payload — treat `startup` as \"first claim wins, dedup against forwarded hooks,\" and treat `resume`/`continue`/`clear`/`compact` as \"always show the banner, this is a fresh user-visible session start.\"\n\nThat keeps (1) and (2) working: forwarded hooks both fire with `source=startup`, so dedup applies; Gemini's startup→resume sequence still dedupes within the same process because the hint is written on the `startup` event and the `resume` event sees it. But `claude -c` enters with `source=resume` and gets the banner."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1137,"cache_read_input_tokens":156745,"output_tokens":1543,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1137,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1543,"cache_read_input_tokens":156745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1137},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Caa1RChXEQzGqfjoibWrT","type":"assistant","uuid":"29775b90-a9c0-43f3-a62c-4c167af93e45","timestamp":"2026-04-30T13:08:38.443Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c3eb3dfd-f856-4fb0-901f-7bae4034e1d7","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"ashtom/cursor-fix"}
