nism\n29\t\n30\t- Config file: `.cursor/hooks.json` (project-local) or `~/.cursor/hooks.json` (user-global)\n31\t- Config format: JSON\n32\t- Hook registration: Array of `{\"command\": \"...\", \"matcher\": \"...\"}` entries per hook type (matcher is optional, used for tool-use hooks)\n33\t\n34\t### Hook Names and When They Fire\n35\t\n36\t| Native Hook Name | When It Fires | Entire EventType | Fires in `-p` mode? |\n37\t|-----------------|---------------|-----------------|---------------------|\n38\t| `sessionStart` | New conversation created | `SessionStart` | Yes |\n39\t| `beforeSubmitPrompt` | After user presses send, before backend request | `TurnStart` | **No** |\n40\t| `stop` | Agent loop ends (one turn completes) | `TurnEnd` | **No** |\n41\t| `sessionEnd` | Conversation ends | `SessionEnd` | Yes |\n42\t| `preCompact` | Before context compaction | `Compaction` | Needs long context |\n43\t| `subagentStart` | Before spawning a subagent (Task tool) | `SubagentStart` | Yes (when subagent used) |\n44\t| `subagentStop` | Subagent completes | `SubagentEnd` | Yes (when subagent used) |\n45\t| `preToolUse` | Before any tool execution | *(not mapped — informational)* | Yes |\n46\t| `postToolUse` | After tool execution | *(not mapped — informational)* | Yes |\n47\t\n48\t### Hook Input (stdin JSON)\n49\t\n50\tAll hooks share these common fields:\n51\t\n52\t```json\n53\t{\n54\t  \"conversation_id\": \"uuid\",\n55\t  \"generation_id\": \"uuid\",\n56\t  \"model\": \"gpt-5.2-codex-xhigh-fast\",\n57\t  \"hook_event_name\": \"sessionStart\",\n58\t  \"cursor_version\": \"2026.02.13-41ac335\",\n59\t  \"workspace_roots\": [\"/path/to/repo\"],\n60\t  \"user_email\": \"user@example.com\",\n61\t  \"transcript_path\": null\n62\t}\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t**Important:** `transcript_path` is **always `null`** in CLI mode. The existing cursor agent handles this via `resolveTranscriptRef()` which computes the path dynamically from the repo root.\n66\t\n67\t#### sessionStart additional fields\